# CODEOWNERS
#
# Patterns are evaluated top-to-bottom (last matching pattern takes precedence). A team that wants to own a folder adds
# a line here in a pull request that wg-infra approves (see the self-protection rule below). Leave a folder out and any
# maintainer's approval is enough.

# CODEOWNERS Self-Protection
/CODEOWNERS @osac-project/wg-infra

# CI pipeline definition
# A pull request can change the workflows and scripts that produce the checks it is judged by, and then a passing check
# proves little. A change to them needs review from the infrastructure team. The E2E starts from the default branch's
# copy of the suite workflows (a pull request's change to them is first exercised in the merge queue), so these files
# need a person who reads them.
/.github/workflows/ @osac-project/wg-infra
/.github/actions/ @osac-project/wg-infra
/.github/scripts/ @osac-project/wg-infra
/.github/filters/ @osac-project/wg-infra
/.github/e2e-policy.yml @osac-project/wg-infra
/.pre-commit-config.yaml @osac-project/wg-infra
